[Event "The Alien Gambit: Alien gambit"]
[Date "2024.09.19"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "B15"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Alien Gambit"]
[StudyName "The Alien Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Alien gambit"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/XvTkesnD/khLJNRRc"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/OneAndOnlyChessGod"]
[UTCDate "2024.09.19"]
[UTCTime "07:23:04"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ In the alien gambit, you open with e4. }
1. e4 c6 { Take the centre. } 2. d4 d5 { Develop the knight } 3. Nd2 dxe4 { Take back. } 4. Nxe4 Nf6 { Threaten the alien gambit on g5. } 5. Ng5 h6 6. Nxf7 Kxf7 { Begin to develop, this is also opening up the king in multiple ways and bringing it towards the centre. } { [%cal Gf1c4,Gg1f3,Gd1h5] } 7. Nf3 e6 { Develop with bd3. } 8. Bd3 Nbd7 { Bring the king to safety. } 9. O-O Bd6 { Develop the rook. } 10. Re1 Re8 { Now you can create a strong attack with the knight, where do you put it? } 11. Ne5+ Bxe5 { Take back. } 12. dxe5 Nd5 { Develop your queen to an attacking square. } 13. Qh5+ Kg8 { Now you can create a very strong attack with yet another sacrifice. } 14. Bxh6!! gxh6 { After queen to g6 it is checkmate no matter what. } { [%cal Gd3h7,Gh5f7,Gh5g6,Gh5h6] } 15. Qg6+ *


[Event "The Alien Gambit: Martian gambit"]
[Date "2024.09.19"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "B18"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Martian Gambit"]
[StudyName "The Alien Gambit"]
[ChapterName "Martian gambit"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/XvTkesnD/feGaxDnw"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/OneAndOnlyChessGod"]
[UTCDate "2024.09.19"]
[UTCTime "11:25:34"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Bring out the pawns like in the alien gambit. }
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 { Play g5 the same as the alien gambit. } 5. Ng5 Bg6 { Protect your knight. } 6. N1f3 h6 { Sacrifice the knight on g5. } 7. Ne6!! fxe6 { Attack the bishop. } 8. Ne5 Bf7 { Develop your bishop. } 9. Bc4 Nd7 { Trade for the bishop, also disallowing castling. } 10. Nxf7 Kxf7 { Queen to g4 threatening to take the pawn and check. This opens up their king. } { [%cal Gd1h5,Gd1f3,Gd1g4,Gc4e6] } 11. Qg4 Qa5+ { Defend with the bishop. } 12. Bd2 Qc7 { Take the free piece. } 13. Bxe6+ Ke8 { Check again, notice how many places there are to attack. } { [%cal Gg4h5,Gg4g6,Ge6d7,Ge6f7,Gd2f4] } 14. Qg6+ Kd8 { Protect your pawn on g2. } 15. O-O Ngf6 { Centralize your rook. } 16. Rfe1 a5 { Attack the queen. } 17. c4 c5 { Take. } 18. dxc5 Nxc5 { Bring the rook to d1, sacraficing your bishop. } 19. Rad1!! Nxe6 { Find the discovered check. } 20. Bxa5+ Kc8 { Take. } 21. Bxc7 Nxc7 { Give another check with the queen for a winning position. } 22. Qf5+ *


